			<div class="content" id="post-content-4853745">
									

<p>So, the problem you have here is that, so far it is impossible to know what you want to do with this idea. The description you gave is a word by word explanation of what the cordyceps fungus does in real life, there is no narrative here. All this post should be placed in the Elevator Pitch area and in the Central Narrative you should write the outline of the story you want to tell, which seems to be about this person infected by the fungus that managed to communicate with a non-infected person. This is not the moment for mysteries, it is important to reveal your hand so the critters can help you develop your idea, once you start writing the draf you can chose what information you will make available to the audience and what ones you will hide for dramatic purposes.<br />
You are still well below the 400 words limit, make good use of the space you have to sell your idea!</p>

