			<div class="content" id="post-content-4853741">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-XXXX represents a single species of fungi, currently only known to exist within northern Queensland, Australia. SCP-XXXX is similar to the genus Ophiocordyceps, as SCP-XXXX has the ability to infect Insectoids, Birds, and Mamalians including Humans. Once an individual has been infected with SCP-XXXX (now designated SCP-XXXX-1) during early stages will begin to suppress the individual's consciousness and hijack the brain. SCP-XXXX has the ability to tap into the memories of SCP-XXXX-1, because of this SCP-XXXX-1 are able to basic human things such as communicating, movement, etc</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> SCP-XXXX during late stages will use the SCP-XXXX-1 instance to move to a suitable location to multiply. Once achieved SCP-XXXX-1 will attach itself to a surface, as well as immobilising itself by placing a cocoon like structure around its body. From here spores will begin to fly out of SCP-XXXX-1, which will multiply SCP-XXXX</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Numerous SCP-XXXX-1 instances have been leaked (and deleted of course) however one was able to communicate directly to an non-infected individual via text. This is where the story will take place.</p>

