<p>I don't want to bea nudge about this, but I also had an idea to make this a joke SCP and I just want to run the idea to see if it's actually funny or if it's just me.</p>
<p>There are multiple instances of SCP-2806, and multiple instances can be designated by number or letter. In this case they are numbered, but that's for the instances when they are not connected to a human, so what if the humans still connected were designated by letter?</p>
<p>So my guy comes in, clearly a Mary Sue, the data entry worker checks the file and sees that about 200 of these guys could be coming through and decides to designate this instance 2806-J just so he can be purposely misfiled as a joke SCP even though he's not a joke. So the real joke is that he's actually totally legit but nobody takes him seriously because of a prank in records and his career is ruined.</p>
<p>I honestly don't know whether that's funny enough to work, so feel free to shoot it down.</p>

