				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rpm842" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6980491); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6980491&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608950306" alt="RPM842" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6980491)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rpm842" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6980491); return false;" >RPM842</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608943608 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Dec 2020 00:46</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-3005/comments/show">SCP-3005</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4853714">
									

<p>One of my absolute favorite SCPs. There's just enough there to piece together the narrative, and it's a good narrative. And it easily has one of the best first person descents into madness I've seen in any horror story, and I've seen a lot of those.</p>
<p>Some possibly spoilery thoughts:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I interpret the light as destroying the metaphysical &quot;anchor&quot; that keeps something squarely in a single reality, making it exist in multiple parallel realities at once, maybe even every possible reality at once. That's why the researcher says they're not ready for &quot;what's out there&quot;; every possible reality in the Foundation's carefully monitored test chambers is much easier to deal with than the chaos of the world outside. This idea fits in with Star Signals, which describes the Fifth World as your ideal version of reality, the universe sculpted by you into your perfect shape. By severing your connection to one single world, the light gives you the freedom to move to any world. But the human mind isn't made for this, and very strange things happen to a person when they do this.</p>
<p>Most assume the 'body' referred to in &quot;Don't worry about the body&quot; must be a corpse, but I think that line should actually be taken as a much more general statement. As in, don't worry about the physical body, the mind is what matters. Given 3005's general effects on human bodies, this seems like solid advice.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Honestly, I love this SCP, along with 1425, so much that I have trouble accepting any other take on the Fifth Church into my personal headcanon, which I suppose is ironic given the subject material.</p>

							</div>

								
					
